      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T15:19:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hope we are not misunderstanding each other. This block is adding warning flags for the C++ compiler only. Whether a flag disables or enables a warning depends of whether or not it starts with `-Wno-`. The first two flags do start that way, and therefore are being disabled. The flag I\u0027m adding starts doesn\u0027t has a `no` prefix, so it is enabling the warning.\n\nRegarding `-Wall`, and `-Weverything`, I have tested locally and I can confirmed those two flags do not enable `-Wunreachable-code-aggressive`",
      "parentUuid": "3bcecc55_0848b4af",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 497,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 497,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "69e12ff60cc94c0c087bda8b375b9567a805be48",
