    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "efcf98f0_314c6297",
        "filename": "gn/skia/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 497,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T16:28:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be very surprising if `-Weverything` failed to enable a warning. Are you entirely sure? It is documented as enabling _every_ warning. https://clang.llvm.org/docs/UsersManual.html#enabling-all-diagnostics\n\nWe generally should not need to enable any additional warning flags at all after `-Weverything` is set, unless we have a `-Wno-feature` which disables a broad set of warning flags; in that case we may need a `-Wsubset-of-feature` to reenable portions of the `feature` that we do want to be warned about.\n\nIs it possible that when you tested this originally, these disables were still present?\n\n```\n      \"-Wno-unreachable-code-break\",\n      \"-Wno-unreachable-code-return\",\n```",
      "parentUuid": "4a2498f2_c709043a",
